		(property "MPN" "OPA2333AIDGKR"
			(at 0 0 90)
			(layer "F.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "5a1d9b58-3d8c-5901-b204-6fe43bd0e004")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Design Note" "Both halves are now unity-gain electrometer followers on the cell nodes: A buffers WE, B buffers RE and drives both the guard (through R40) and the ADC bias telemetry. Half A was freed by deleting the VREF trim divider. NO FEMTOAMPERE PART IS NEEDED HERE and this is the reason: SBOS351E gives OPA333 IB as +/-70 pA typ and +/-200 pA max at 25 C. MIND THE ARITHMETIC: IB is the AVERAGE of the two inputs, and a follower's electrode sees the non-inverting input alone, so the real bound is |IB| + |IOS|/2 = 200 + 200 = 400 pA. The RE node is ALREADY loaded by the LMP91000's own RE pin at +/-90 pA typ and +/-900 pA max over -40..80 C (SNAS506I IRE, TI's own front-page feature; at this board's 3.3 V the applicable column is nearer 800 pA). So half B takes RE's worst case from ~900 pA to ~1300 pA, +44%, and an ADA4530-1 at 20 fA would still leave ~900 pA and buy nothing. UNSTATED ASSUMPTION, flagged deliberately: SBOS351E gives NO max for IB over temperature, only +/-150 pA typ, so the claim that a chopper's charge-injection-dominated bias stays flat to 75 C rests on Figure 8, a typical curve, not a guaranteed limit. See POTTING.md section 1.3 under ../../../ha/farming/compostlab/o2-probe/"
			(at 0 0 90)
			(layer "F.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "032d026d-49f6-5cbb-9ef6-68c676ac4a62")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
