		(property "KiLib_Generator" "SMD_2terminal_chip_molded"
			(at 0 0 0)
			(layer "B.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "f1b1f351-d4b4-41e4-b72b-f8468bc85af9")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
				(justify mirror)
			)
		)
		(property "Design Note" "REV B.  The failsafe that makes the RE split SAFE, and it is the whole reason the split is not dangerous.  RE is active low with a 2 MOhm internal pull-UP, so an undriven RE pin is a DISABLED receiver -- and every MCU GPIO is high-impedance out of reset.  Without this resistor a probe that reset into the RS-485 bootloader (loader_main.c / loader_uart.c) would come up DEAF, destroying the field-reflash path SCHEMATIC-REVIEW.md M2 exists to provide.  A potted probe would be unrecoverable.  R45 makes receiver-enabled the passive default exactly as R7 makes driver-disabled the passive default.\nARITHMETIC.  Size against the GUARANTEED spec, not the 2 MOhm typical: SLLSEY3E gives IIN = +/-6.2 uA max for D, DE and RE over 3 V <= VCC <= 5.5 V, with VIL max 0.8 V.  So the largest pull-down that still guarantees a low is R <= 0.8 V / 6.2 uA = 129k.\n  47k: worst case 6.2 uA * 47k = 291 mV, a 2.75x margin to VIL.  (The 2 MOhm typical would give 76 mV, but a typical is not a guarantee and this pin must never come up deaf.)\nCOST, stated plainly because it bounds the win this split was made for: commanding standby means DRIVING RE high, which pushes 3.3 V / 47k = 70.2 uA through R45.  Standby is therefore ~70 uA, not the part's 0.1 uA.  Against the 700 uA receiver that is still a 10x cut (630 uA saved), but it is NOT the 7000x the datasheet row promises, and at the duty-cycled floor of ~29 uA in POWER-BUDGET.md this resistor would be the single largest load on the board.\nWHY NOT A WEAKER PULL-DOWN: the 129k ceiling above means no resistor can better ~26 uA, so 220k/470k do not trade margin for microamps -- they are simply OUT OF SPEC (220k worst case = 1.36 V, 470k = 2.9 V, both above VIL).  A resistor structurally cannot reach the 0.1 uA this split was made for; only omitting R45 and having the loader drive RE low early can, and that trades a sub-ms deaf window after reset.  Fab chose 47k, 2026-09-07: robust, passive, no init-order dependency."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(layer "B.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "ba1d1687-6a07-4c1c-9e1d-77163865e5e5")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "ki_keywords" "R res resistor"
			(at 0 0 0)
			(layer "B.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "e29e2a96-8951-4e47-bd8f-8621d0a758c1")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
